// THE THREE CALL SHAPES v1 ACCEPTS AND §2.2 HAD NO NUMBER FOR -- assigned by
// the author 2026-09-09, and one of them was blocking M20's own done-when:
// example/full_test.satl:613 is satellite.system.memory.this.used("kb"), a
// shape this file did not carry. v1's unit block is reached for every swap and
// `this` form, so it answers .swap.used(unit) and .this.used(unit) while §2.2
// wrote 1 22 4 4 3 and 1 22 4 5 3 without the parens their siblings carry --
// the table recording a sweep's arity rather than the code.
//
// `environment(name)` IS A SIBLING AND NOT A CHILD, which is §4's rule and not
// a preference: a USER-owned argument contributes no number of its own, so its
// call shape takes a slot beside its siblings. memory.main() 1 22 4 3 against
// main(unit) 1 22 4 9, six slots apart, is the same rule already in the table.
// The bare `environment` 1 22 2 answers a map of the whole environment and this
// one answers the single variable -- the same read-all / read-one pair
// satellite.system.memory carries.
SAT_NODE(SYSTEM,             SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_NAME,           "environment(name)", SAT_NUMBERED)  // 1 22 9

